// Which pictures of the original's art (`assets-local/art`) belong to which spell. A picture is
// its source file and entry (`lbx`, `entry`) and what it is for (`role`, see `Role` in
// `crates/f4x-data/src/spell_art.rs`). `extract-art` files a picture of one spell under
// `art/spells/<spell id>/`, one used by several spells or listed under `shared` under
// `art/spells/_shared/`. The client reads the pictures to draw from here; how an animation moves
// stays in `spell_fx.rs`. Sources: ReMoM's `Spell_Animation_Load_Graphics` and the tables in
// `docs/overland_spell_animations.md`.
(
    shared: [
        (lbx: "specfx", entry: 0, role: Realm("nature")),
        (lbx: "specfx", entry: 1, role: Realm("sorcery")),
        (lbx: "specfx", entry: 2, role: Realm("chaos")),
        (lbx: "specfx", entry: 3, role: Realm("life")),
        (lbx: "specfx", entry: 4, role: Realm("death")),
        (lbx: "specfx", entry: 5, role: Realm("arcane")),
        (lbx: "cmbtfx", entry: 22, role: Summon),
        (lbx: "spellscr", entry: 46, role: SummonBackground(0)),
        (lbx: "spellscr", entry: 47, role: SummonBackground(1)),
        (lbx: "spellscr", entry: 48, role: SummonBackground(2)),
        (lbx: "spellscr", entry: 49, role: SummonBackground(3)),
